---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About — aivan.io"
  description="About Aivan Monceller: a Singapore-based software engineer and tool builder working on interfaces, developer tooling, local AI, and coding agents."
  keywords={['aivan monceller', 'about']}
>
  <div class="row rowt">
    <div class="gl hd">
      <h1 class="term">Aivan Monceller</h1>
      <div class="hero-rail-meta">
        <span class="rl">software builder</span>
        <span class="rl">singapore ⇄ philippines</span>
        <span class="status-pill">
          <span class="status-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <span>razer inc. · UI/UX</span>
        </span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="gr hd about-body">
      <p class="hero-eyebrow">DOSSIER // PERSONAL LOG</p>
      <h1 class="dtitle">Hi, I’m Aivan.</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        I’m a software engineer, tool builder, and lifelong tinkerer based in
        Singapore.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="row">
    <div class="gl about-note-rail">
      <span class="marginalia-tag">01 / trajectory</span>
      <span class="marginalia-sub">frontend systems → device protocols → local AI</span>
    </div>
    <div class="gr about-body about-block prose">
      <p>
        I’ve spent most of my career around interfaces and developer-facing
        software, but I tend to wander wherever the interesting problems are.
        That has taken me from frontend systems and device software to
        developer tooling, infrastructure, local AI, model training, and
        lately, a lot of thinking about how software changes when AI becomes
        part of the development process itself.
      </p>
      <p>
        These days I work as a frontend/UI engineer at Razer, building
        software that sits between people and hardware. Outside of work, I’m
        usually building something of my own: coding agents, developer tools,
        AI infrastructure, terminal experiments, training pipelines, or
        whatever idea I can’t stop thinking about that week.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="row">
    <div class="gl about-note-rail">
      <span class="marginalia-tag">02 / philosophy</span>
      <span class="marginalia-sub">abstractions, workflows &amp; tactile craft</span>
    </div>
    <div class="gr about-body about-block prose">
      <p>
        I’m especially interested in tools that make complicated systems feel
        simple. Not just making something technically work, but figuring out
        the interface, abstractions, workflow, and little details that make
        someone actually want to use it.
      </p>
      <p>
        AI has changed how I work quite a bit. I write less code by hand than
        I used to, and spend more time designing systems, directing agents,
        reviewing decisions, building feedback loops, and figuring out where
        human judgment still matters. After many years of programming, I find
        that shift more interesting than threatening. It feels like learning
        the craft again with different materials.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="row">
    <div class="gl about-note-rail">
      <span class="marginalia-tag">03 / this notebook</span>
      <span class="marginalia-sub">working notes &amp; half-formed ideas</span>
    </div>
    <div class="gr about-body about-block prose">
      <p>
        This site is where I keep track of that process.
      </p>
      <p>
        I write about things I’m building, things I’m learning, experiments
        that worked, experiments that didn’t, and ideas that are still
        half-formed. It’s less of a portfolio and more of a public notebook
        for the things I normally don’t get enough chances to talk about.
      </p>
      <p>
        Away from building software, I’m usually playing games, messing with
        hardware, listening to music, or going down another rabbit hole that
        will probably turn into a project.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="row rowt">
    <div class="gl sp">
      <h2 class="slab">colophon</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="gr sp about-body">
      <div class="field-matrix">
        <div class="matrix-cell">
          <span class="matrix-kicker">now // building</span>
          <ul class="matrix-list">
            <li><span>device interfaces</span><span class="m-dim">razer</span></li>
            <li><span>coding agents</span><span class="m-dim">lab</span></li>
            <li><span>local AI / candle</span><span class="m-dim">rust</span></li>
            <li><span>cli &amp; dev tools</span><span class="m-dim">oss</span></li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="matrix-cell">
          <span class="matrix-kicker">materials // stack</span>
          <ul class="matrix-list">
            <li><span>typescript / react</span><span class="m-dim">ui</span></li>
            <li><span>rust / python / go</span><span class="m-dim">sys</span></li>
            <li><span>astro + shiki</span><span class="m-dim">site</span></li>
            <li><span>gloss-v2 grid</span><span class="m-dim">spec</span></li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
